# Suricata settings for OT visibility. Append to <malcolm>/config/suricata.env.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# Malcolm's generator (suricata/scripts/suricata_config_populate.py) reads
# SURICATA_* environment variables and writes suricata.yaml from them. Three of
# its settings decide whether OT detection works and what it produces:
#
#   MODBUS_ENABLED / DNP3_ENABLED        the application-layer parsers.
#                                        Required: the Suricata rule keyword
#                                        `modbus: function 6` matches nothing
#                                        without the parser, so the OT rules
#                                        silently never fire.
#   MODBUS_EVE_ENABLED / DNP3_EVE_ENABLED
#                                        the `modbus` / `dnp3` eve-log event
#                                        types. Optional: alerts fire without
#                                        them, but the protocol transaction
#                                        records that hunting, Arkime and the
#                                        dashboards read are missing.
#   DISABLE_ICS_ALL                      a master switch. Malcolm's
#                                        config/suricata.env sets it, and
#                                        turning it on disables every ICS parser
#                                        at once, with no rule change and no
#                                        alert. It is the setting most likely to
#                                        be flipped by someone hardening the
#                                        sensor.
#
# The generator decides each eve-log type with:
#
#   enabled = (type == 'alert') or (PROTOCOLS[type].enabled and PROTOCOLS[type].eve_enabled)
#
# so `alert` is always on and the protocol event types follow the two switches.
# Alert records carry their application-layer detail through a separate setting,
# METADATA_ALERT_APP_LAYER_EVE_ENABLED, which defaults to true — which is why an
# alert shows its Modbus fields even with the protocol event type disabled.
#
# deployment/verify_deployment.py proves the load-bearing part: with the parser
# off there are no alerts, with it on there is one.
#
# Install
# -------
#   cat suricata.env.fragment >> <malcolm>/config/suricata.env
#   cd <malcolm> && docker compose up -d --force-recreate suricata suricata-live

# ICS parsing must not be globally disabled.
SURICATA_DISABLE_ICS_ALL=false

# Modbus: parse (required for detection) and emit transaction records.
SURICATA_MODBUS_ENABLED=true
SURICATA_MODBUS_EVE_ENABLED=true
SURICATA_MODBUS_PORTS=502

# DNP3: parse (required for detection) and emit transaction records.
SURICATA_DNP3_ENABLED=true
SURICATA_DNP3_EVE_ENABLED=true
SURICATA_DNP3_PORTS=20000

# EtherNet/IP is also an ICS protocol Malcolm can parse. The ruleset in
# ot-detection-engineering does not cover it; uncomment if that changes.
# SURICATA_ENIP_ENABLED=true
# SURICATA_ENIP_EVE_ENABLED=true
